Note that this code does not include advanced features such as distributed data storage, concurrent access handling, error recovery, or optimized I/O operations for large files. It serves as a starting point for learning basic memory management and synchronization techniques in C. For more complex systems, additional layers of abstraction, concurrency control mechanisms, and specialized libraries would be necessary.']

