using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Data;
using System.Data.SqlClient;

public class DynamicSQLQueryExecutor
{
    public static DataTable ExecuteDynamicQuery(string connectionString, string baseSqlCommandTemplate, List<FilterCriteria> filters)
    {
        using (SqlConnection connection = new SqlConnection(connectionString))
        {
            using (SqlCommand command = new SqlCommand(baseSqlCommandTemplate, connection))
            {
                foreach (var filter in filters)
                {
                    command.Parameters.AddWithValue($"@{filter.PropertyName}", filter.Value);
                }

                SqlDataAdapter adapter = new SqlDataAdapter(command);
                DataTable resultTable = new DataTable();
                adapter.Fill(resultTable);

                return resultTable;
            }
        }
    }
}

public class FilterCriteria
{
    public string PropertyName { get; set; }
    public object Value { get; set; }
}
```

This code snippet provides a basic implementation of the `ExecuteDynamicQuery` method, which takes a connection string, a base SQL command template, and a list of filter criteria. Each filter criterion includes a property name and a value, which are dynamically added as parameters to the SQL command to prevent SQL injection and ensure type safety. The `SqlDataAdapter` is then used to fill a `DataTable` with the query results.

The `FilterCriteria` class is a simple data structure used to encapsulate the filter criteria for each dynamic parameter in the SQL query. This design allows the method to be flexible, handle various data types, and scale to support concurrent requests without compromising performance or data integrity.']

